The following complete solution.py has one semantic bug. Return a corrected complete source file implementing `summarize_events(events) -> tuple[str, ...]`.

`events` must be a non-string iterable of mappings. Each mapping must have a string `type`. Supported types are:
- `key_down` and `key_up`, requiring a non-empty string `key`;
- `move`, requiring integer `x` and `y` values other than booleans;
- `button`, requiring a non-negative integer `number` other than boolean and a boolean `pressed`;
- `quit`, requiring no other fields.

Unknown types or extra fields raise `ValueError`; missing fields raise `KeyError`; other malformed values raise `TypeError` or `ValueError`. Process events in input order. Emit respectively `DOWN key`, `UP key`, `MOVE x,y`, and `BUTTON number DOWN|UP`. A `quit` event emits nothing and immediately stops processing, so later events are neither validated nor summarized. Empty input returns an empty tuple. Do not mutate input events.

